Looking at this problem, I need to compute the expected value of f(s)² where f(s) counts positions where prefix equals suffix.

Let me derive the formula:
- Let X_i be indicator that prefix of length i equals suffix of length i
- f(s) = ∑X_i, so E[f(s)²] = E[(∑X_i)²] = ∑E[X_i²] + ∑_{i≠j} E[X_i X_j]
- Since X_i is indicator, X_i² = X_i, so E[X_i²] = P(X_i=1) = (1/k)ⁱ
- For E[X_i X_j], if gcd(i,j) = g, the overlap is at g positions, so P = (1/k)ᵍ

The formula becomes:
E[f(s)²] = ∑_{i=1}^{n-1} (1/k)ⁱ + ∑_{i≠j} (1/k)^{gcd(i,j)}

Grouping by gcd: ∑_{g=1}^{n-1} (1/k)ᵍ × count{pairs with gcd=i,j=g}

For pairs with gcd(i,j)=g, let i=ag, j=bg with gcd(a,b)=1 and 1≤a<b≤(n-1)/g. Count = ∑_{b=2}^{(n-1)/g} φ(b)

